; Redraw cells: length of the run that starts at this cell
;
; One byte per queued cell, indexed like #R$C400 and #R$C500. Only the entry of the first cell of a run is meaningful:
; it holds the number of cells in the run (#R$976B writes it, #R$95FF reads it). Observed after a frame: runs of 1 to
; 7 cells.
@label=RedrawLengths
g$C300 DEFS $0100,$FF ;
